From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:59:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] squash! wpt: Add the QuickJS expectations

Drop the QuickJS conditions of the media tests that failed because
nothing kept unreferenced media elements alive: autoplay.html,
allowed-to-play.html, resource-selection-candidate-moved.html and the
autoplay-allowed-by and autoplay-default permissions policy tests. Patch 69
fixes that, and QuickJS gives SpiderMonkey's results for them now.
Patch 69 drops the conditions of autoplay-disabled-by-permissions-policy
itself, because it edits that file after this one.

Validation: QuickJS release build of this branch, `./mach test-wpt --js-engine quickjs --processes 2` of these tests, autoplay-disabled-by-permissions-policy, played-loop and the new gc-unreferenced-media-element.html, 2 runs: all as expected for SpiderMonkey, apart from autoplay-default-permissions-policy, which is OK on this host with either engine against its TIMEOUT expectation; without patches 68 to 70 the QuickJS build times out in these tests as the dropped conditions expected.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; validated and written by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
